RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,RST$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315832 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315833 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315834 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315835 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315836 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1041 "selection" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315835 13194139534865 true] [17592186315831 1110 #uuid "1c7975e9-aae5-5e69-b729-ce54b2077f4b" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315832 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315832 1111 #uuid "638bcb65-4122-545a-ab06-ad87df9711dd" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315833 1034 "2" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315833 1111 #uuid "d370cbf3-f6d5-5fb7-9cce-d7bdc54e937d" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315834 1034 "1" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315834 1111 #uuid "52c45163-2b9b-59d1-a134-45161212a4ac" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315835 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315835 1111 #uuid "887ac26f-bc26-50ec-a1f8-505dcb2986d7" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315836 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315836 1111 #uuid "a102e698-0608-50bf-a7cc-5514dd47d512" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315838 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1089 "q-316362" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1100 "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-2,1,3)$, $E(0,-1,0)$, $F(2,2,-1).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1113 #uuid "373c3c2a-c3be-590c-bc9b-26aa9142940c" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315837 1145 "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =(-j)-(-2i+j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-2j-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(2i+2j-k)-(-2i+j+3k) \\\\  & =4i+j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-4)-(-3)\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-4)-(-3)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =11i-4j+10k \\\\  & =⟨11,-4,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+16+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{237}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DEF$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{237}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315839 13194139534865 true] [17592186315838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534865 true] [17592186315838 1041 "field-1" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315839 13194139534865 true] [17592186315838 1110 #uuid "338620ed-0add-56e9-9f00-a288492f8ce6" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315839 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{237}}{2}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315839 1111 #uuid "c36e1f16-7336-50e3-8771-9e0bd612d7f9" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315841 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1089 "q-316409" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1100 "Calculate the length of the altitude $IP$ of the $△\\,HIJ$, if $H(-1,2,0)$, $I(1,1,3)$, $J(0,-2,1).$\n\n$IP=${{field-1}}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1113 #uuid "1e929d09-28f2-5088-a9e8-afcb5cdf64da" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315840 1145 "Note that the length of the altitude $IP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,HIJ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $IP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ} & =j-h \\\\  & =(-2j+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =i-4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =i-h \\\\  & =(i+j+3k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-11i-j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-11,-1,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{171} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,HIJ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $HJ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}HJ & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,IP\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,IP \\\\ IP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315842 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315843 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1041 "field-1" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315842 13194139534865 true] [17592186315841 1110 #uuid "a9028da6-1499-5ed9-92f0-b5c25697381f" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315842 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315842 1111 #uuid "15ea403b-a3b7-5823-805c-83dd5f0a467e" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315843 1034 "\\sqrt{38}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534865 true] [17592186315843 1111 #uuid "549549a3-b5e7-56df-b0f0-96ad058949be" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315845 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1089 "q-316553" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1100 "Calculate the length of the altitude $CK$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(1,0,1),$ $B(4,2,1),$ $C(2,3,2).$\n\n$CK=${{field-1}}" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1113 #uuid "5fd17faa-9755-51af-bf8a-e34a38cc6648" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315844 1145 "Note that the length of the altitude $CK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+2j+k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+0k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+2k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)i-(3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1)j+(3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-3j+7k \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot \\sqrt{13} \\\\ CK & =\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ CK & =\\frac{\\sqrt{806}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534865 true] [17592186315845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315846 13194139534865 true] [17592186315845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534865 true] [17592